issue_context.body:
### What happened?

A patch was applied using client-go:

```
rawPatch := `
{
  "apiVersion":"apps/v1",
  "kind":"Deployment",
  "metadata":{
    "labels":{
      "app":"metrics-forwarder"
    },
    "name":"metrics-forwarder-deployment-1"
  },
  "spec":{
    "replicas":1,
    "selector":{
      "matchLabels":{
        "app":"metrics-forwarder"
      }
    },
    "template":{
      "metadata":{
        "labels":{
          "app":"metrics-forwarder"
        }
      },
      "spec":{
        "nodeAffinity":{
          "preferredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution":[
            {
              "preference":{
                "matchExpressions":[
                  {
                    "key":"XXXXX",
                    "operator":"In",
                    "values":[
                      "true"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              "weight":50
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
`

patch := client.RawPatch(types.ApplyPatchType, []byte(rawPatch))
dst := obj.DeepCopyObject().(*unstructured.Unstructured)
err := p.client.Patch(ctx, dst, patch, client.DryRunAll)
```

Please note that the patch contains the key `spec.template.spec.nodeAffinity` while it should correctly be `spec.template.spec.affinity.nodeAffinity` .

`err` returned is of type APIStatus, its `Status()` method returns
```
{"kind":"Status","apiVersion":"v1","metadata":{},"status":"Failure","message":"failed to create typed patch object (XXXX/metrics-forwarder-deployment-1; apps/v1, Kind=Deployment): .spec.template.spec.nodeAffinity: field not declared in schema","code":500}
```

Note that the `Reason` field is empty.

### What did you expect to happen?

The reason field of the returned status should not be empty. I personally would have expected `StatusReasonInvalid` or `StatusReasonBadRequest`.

### How can we reproduce it (as minimally and precisely as possible)?

Create and apply a patch that contains key that are not part of the schema of the patched object.

### Anything else we need to know?

